      children: [(0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(_components.strong, {
        children: "Osho Darshan:"
      }), " The three austerities — body, word, mind — become one when they are done with supreme faith and no bargaining. Osho would say: this is the definition of the integrated man — his body, his speech and his mind all move in the same direction, the direction of awareness. Such a man is \"yukta\" — united, disciplined, in accord. And the faith is supreme — not faith in a reward, but faith in the rightness of the discipline itself. The sattvic austerity is its own fruit; it needs no future prize because its present is already fulfilled. Watch: any discipline that makes you anxious for its result is still rajasic; the sattvic discipline is its own quiet joy."]
